    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.64–0.67 from 7 h onward, right after fast growth. That looks like reader saturation, not a real stationary phase. The 18 h aliquot read 0.2513 at 10× dilution, which is 2.51 after scaling. At 25× dilution it read 0.0915, which is 2.29 after scaling. Both scaled values are about 3.5–4 times the undiluted reading of 0.644, so the undiluted reading is not proportional to biomass. The 25× value is likely the more reliable one, because it sits further into the linear range. The 10× value may still be slightly compressed. I estimate the true 18 h OD at about 2.3–2.5 and used 2.3."
